From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:45:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: ipq95xx: c-460: light the radio LEDs

The 2.4, 5 and 6 GHz LEDs had no trigger. The three QCN9224 radios
register in a different order from boot to boot, so their phy numbers
change even on one unit, and board.d cannot name them. A hotplug script
ties each LED to its radio by device path instead, with the radio's
phyNradio trigger: the LED is lit while the radio is enabled. pcie1 is
the 2.4 GHz radio, pcie3 the 5 GHz radio and pcie2 the 6 GHz radio
("5g_6g" in the vendor firmware). The QCN9074 scan radio on pcie0 has
no LED.

Tested on a unit, from RAM: with an AP on each QCN9224 the three LEDs
are on, after wifi down they are off; on that boot pcie1 was phy3, pcie3
phy1 and pcie2 phy2.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 .../hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-460-leds  | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-460-leds

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-460-leds b/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-460-leds
new file mode 100755
index 00000000000..25e7fc708f0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-460-leds
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Arista C-460: each radio LED follows its radio, found by device path.
+# The ath12k radios register in a different order from boot to boot, so
+# their phy numbers cannot name them. pcie1 is the 2.4 GHz radio, pcie3
+# the 5 GHz radio and pcie2 the 6 GHz radio ("5g_6g" in the vendor
+# firmware). The QCN9074 on pcie0 is the scan radio and has no LED.
+# "phyNradio" lights the LED while the radio is enabled.
+
+[ "$ACTION" = add ] || exit 0
+
+. /lib/functions.sh
+
+[ "$(board_name)" = arista,c-460 ] || exit 0
+
+case "$(readlink "/sys/class/ieee80211/$DEVICENAME/device")" in
+*/0001:01:00.0)
+	led=green:wlan-2ghz
+	;;
+*/0003:01:00.0)
+	led=green:wlan-5ghz
+	;;
+*/0002:01:00.0)
+	led=green:wlan-6ghz
+	;;
+*)
+	exit 0
+	;;
+esac
+
+echo "${DEVICENAME}radio" > "/sys/class/leds/$led/trigger"
-- 
